From af8d1e3bde76c7fa45fcd9cc56e3ec39b780b171 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ramin Moussavi <ramin.moussavi@yacoub.de>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:28:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sparc32: treat PAGE_NONE ptes as present

SRMMU_PAGE_NONE has no SRMMU_VALID, so that every access to a PROT_NONE
page faults, but pte_present() only looks at that bit.  A PROT_NONE pte
of a populated page is therefore neither pte_none() nor pte_present(),
which is how the core mm recognises a swap entry.  mprotect(), fork()
and munmap() then treat the page as swapped out: "Bad swap file entry"
and "Bad rss-counter state" in the log, a warning in __swap_duplicate()
or zap_pte_range(), SIGBUS on the next access, and after a few rounds
"kernel BUG at include/linux/swapops.h:504" in copy_page_range(), after
which the machine hangs.

Report such a pte as present.  It is told apart from a swap pte by its
access bits: a swap pte has bits 0-5 clear, a PAGE_NONE pte has
SRMMU_PRIV.  Test only SRMMU_PRIV_RDONLY, because SRMMU_WRITE is part of
SRMMU_PRIV and pte_wrprotect() clears it when fork() write-protects a
COW mapping.

Found with a uClibc-ng test that makes a populated page PROT_NONE and
forks; it hung leon3 under qemu after a few runs.  A reproducer that
populates a page, makes it PROT_NONE, forks and reads the page back
after mprotect(PROT_READ) gets SIGBUS on the first round without this
change.  With it, on a 4-CPU SPARCstation 20 (next-20261014) and on
leon3 (v6.18.37), the reproducer passes 200 rounds, the uClibc-ng test
1800 runs, and the uClibc-ng test suite shows no new failures.

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Ramin Moussavi <ramin.moussavi@yacoub.de>
---
 arch/sparc/include/asm/pgtable_32.h | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/include/asm/pgtable_32.h b/arch/sparc/include/asm/pgtable_32.h
index 749bed304efe..e31bd92faa52 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/include/asm/pgtable_32.h
+++ b/arch/sparc/include/asm/pgtable_32.h
@@ -133,9 +133,18 @@ static inline pmd_t *pud_pgtable(pud_t pud)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * A PAGE_NONE pte has no SRMMU_VALID, so that the MMU faults on every
+ * access, but the page is still mapped.  It is told apart from a swap pte
+ * by its access bits, SRMMU_PRIV, which a swap pte (bits 0-5 clear) never
+ * has.  Only SRMMU_PRIV_RDONLY is tested: SRMMU_WRITE is part of
+ * SRMMU_PRIV, and pte_wrprotect() clears it, as fork does on a COW
+ * mapping.
+ */
 static inline int pte_present(pte_t pte)
 {
-	return ((pte_val(pte) & SRMMU_ET_MASK) == SRMMU_ET_PTE);
+	return (pte_val(pte) & SRMMU_ET_MASK) == SRMMU_ET_PTE ||
+	       (pte_val(pte) & SRMMU_PRIV_RDONLY) == SRMMU_PRIV_RDONLY;
 }
 
 static inline int pte_none(pte_t pte)
-- 
